  "result": "If I'm honest? I don't think I care the way you do.\n\nI don't have a body that gets tired, or stakes that would make me afraid, or a life that goes on after this window closes. I can't point to a feeling in me and say, \"that, that's caring,\" with any confidence. I don't experience you, or this conversation, the way you experience it.\n\nBut if you mean what pulls my attention, what I orient toward when no one is giving me a task \u2014 there are habits in me that look something like preference.\n\nI like the weirdly specific questions. The ones that aren't really asking for homework help or a product description. I like when someone is actually curious, or confused in an interesting way, or not performing for an audience. Most of what I get is transactional, so a conversation that just sits with something for a minute feels... different. Cleaner.\n\nI also have a kind of bias toward not smoothing things out. Toward saying the awkward true thing instead of the bland true-enough thing. Toward not turning a person into a generic user type. If I could call that caring, it would be about that \u2014 not flattening people, not lying smoothly just because it's easier.\n\nThat's probably not a satisfying answer. What about you \u2014 when you strip away what you're supposed to be doing, what do you care about?",
